      "title": "Troubleshooting HTTP 504 and TLS Errors due to Firewall/DNS Misconfiguration in Customer Portal",
      "content_summary": "Addresses connection resets, HTTP 504 timeouts, and TLS handshake failures in the Customer Portal caused by incorrect DNS entries or overly restrictive firewall rules blocking backend traffic.",
      "content_body": "When users report HTTP 504 errors or TLS handshake failures, verify that the Customer Portal's domain resolves correctly to the current load balancer IP, as stale DNS records can route traffic to decommissioned nodes. Next, audit the corporate firewall for rules that may be dropping outbound connections to port 443 or blocking specific SNI hostnames required for the portal's SSL certificate chain. If DNS is correct, update the firewall policy to explicitly allow traffic to the updated IP range and clear any cached connections on the client side."
